Accept and propagate `context.Context` across blocking work. Give each goroutine,
channel, timer, and resource a clear owner and shutdown path; bound concurrency
and release resources on every return path. Preserve error identity when wrapping
and use `errors.Is` or `errors.As` for classification. Avoid panic for expected
operational failures and broad recovery that conceals defects.

Make retry safety, idempotency, and resource limits explicit where applicable.
Keep telemetry structured, optional for library consumers, and low-cardinality;
do not put request IDs or other unbounded values into metric labels or policy keys.
Keep observability adapters separate from core logic and test event semantics
when callers depend on them.
